  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>)</mo></math> be the centroid of the triangle formed by the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>82</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#946;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math> are the roots of the equation"
  },
